# Git LFS policy: NOT USED
#
# All binary assets in this repository are under 10MB and are managed
# as normal Git blobs. Git LFS is intentionally not used because:
#   1. git-lfs is not available in this build environment
#   2. All committed binaries are well under GitHub's 100MB/file limit
#   3. The workflow's `lfs: true` checkout would fetch pointer files
#      instead of real content if LFS were half-configured
#
# If a future asset exceeds 50MB, set up Git LFS properly:
#   1. Install git-lfs locally and on all runner images
#   2. Add specific path patterns below (not wildcards)
#   3. Migrate with `git lfs migrate import`
#   4. Verify with `git lfs ls-files` before pushing
#
# The workflow's audio mux step checks for LFS pointer files
# and fails closed if one is found instead of real audio.
